{
  "name": "Calendar",
  "description": "Opens time on a resource a claim books: a stylist, a chair, a room, a collection counter, a pool of bikes. Weekly opening hours in an IANA time zone, which an instance may set for itself, less its closures, give the times a hold may take; capacity says how many holds may overlap. A claim takes time only through the supply contract's operations, which Holds invokes by name: holdFor holds an interval an item of the claim asks, commitFor books it for good and releaseFor frees it. Each checks the claim's own Holds.items, so no caller holds or frees time by calling one directly, and each is idempotent. holdFor refuses an interval outside the hours or in a closure, off the start grid, too short or too long, too soon or too far ahead by the engine's clock, or beyond capacity at any instant, buffers included. findAvailability answers free slots across the schema's instances by the same rules. Wall times become instants through a time zone database the engine carries, so every server built from one lock file computes the same slots; a wall time a daylight-saving change skips has no slot. An instance is not deleted while it holds time for a claim. Calendar and Stock declare the same contract operations, so a type composes one of them.",
